    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d977">

                <pb facs="1035" n="749" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg749"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/3335</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the Treasury</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">McAdoo</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 7, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith a
                    copy of a letter dated the 6th instant from the collector of customs at New
                    York, and the <pb facs="1036" n="750" xml:id="pg750"/> affidavit and memorandum
                    enclosed therewith, relative to the armament of the S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Giuseppe Verdi</hi>, of the Transatlantica-Italiana
                        Line.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d977-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>The collector reports that the steamer has mounted in her stern two 76 millimeter
                    Armstrong guns, with a hundred rounds of ammunition for each gun.</p>
                <p>I will thank you to advise me as soon as possible whether or not this vessel
                    shall be permitted to clear with the armament referred to.</p>
                <p>By direction of the Secretary.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. J. Peters</hi>
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Assistant Secretary</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
